> f(x: real in -10..10) = 1/x where x > 5
> domain f
domain of f:
  x: real
  where x > 5
  requires x != 0  (in 1/x)
  defined on (numerically, grid of 20001 over [-10, 10]):
    x in [5.001, 10]
    except x ≈ 0  (x = 0)
> g(x: real in -10..10) = 1/(x-1) where x < -2
> domain g
domain of g:
  x: real
  where x < -2
  requires x - 1 != 0  (in 1/(x - 1))
  defined on (numerically, grid of 20001 over [-10, 10]):
    x in [-10, -2.001]
    except x ≈ 1  (x - 1 = 0)
> h(x: real in 0..1) = 1/(x-0.5) where x < 0.2
> domain h
domain of h:
  x: real
  where x < 0.2
  requires x - 0.5 != 0  (in 1/(x - 0.5))
  defined on (numerically, grid of 20001 over [0, 1]):
    x in [0, 0.19995]
    except x ≈ 0.5  (x - 0.5 = 0)
